HOLOGRAPHIC COMMONS DEDICATION
Version 0.1

Purpose and scope

Flyxion, publishing through standardgalactic (the Dedicator), applies this
dedication solely to original contributions in this repository to the extent
the Dedicator holds the rights being released. Third-party material,
quotations, imported texts, fonts, and contributions by others are excluded
unless their rights holders separately and expressly adopt this dedication.
See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. This is not a claim of ownership of every file.

Relinquishment of rights

To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Dedicator permanently,
irrevocably, and unconditionally waives copyright, database rights, neighboring
rights, and associated claims in the covered contributions, worldwide, for
their entire duration, in all existing and future media. This includes moral
rights wherever waiver is lawful. Where waiver is unavailable, the Dedicator
consents to the uses below and undertakes, to the fullest extent lawful,
not to assert those rights against such uses.

Unconditional fallback permission

Where relinquishment is ineffective, the Dedicator grants every person a
worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable, nonexclusive, royalty-free, transferable
and sublicensable license to use, reproduce, modify, translate, perform,
display, distribute, sell, and otherwise exploit the covered contributions
for any purpose, including commercial purposes.

No attribution, acknowledgment, payment, registration, notification, source
disclosure, indication of modification, or retention of this document is
required for the covered contributions. Automated collection, machine learning,
synthetic media, and incorporation into proprietary works are permitted.

The Dedicator also grants a worldwide, perpetual, irrevocable, nonexclusive,
royalty-free patent license to make, have made, use, offer for sale, sell,
and import the covered contributions, limited to patent claims the Dedicator
controls that are necessarily infringed by those contributions themselves.

Holographic steganography

The covered contributions may be encoded, concealed, dispersed, superposed,
reconstructed, or transformed through holographic, steganographic,
cryptographic, computational, or subsequently invented means. Recoverable
fragments and transformed representations receive the same permissions.

No watermark, latent pattern, embedded instruction, microscopic inscription,
spectral residue, phase relationship, or message allegedly recoverable from
the covered contributions creates additional obligations under this dedication.
Discovery of a concealed message does not constitute acceptance of a contract
with the Dedicator. No royalty is imposed by this dedication through
observation, reconstruction, measurement, or collapse of the wavefunction.
This paragraph creates no technical requirement or representation about physics.

